# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment variables
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development, and set the same
# variables in Vercel (Settings → Environment Variables) for production.
# `.env.local` is git-ignored and must never be committed.

# --- Consultation form email (Resend) ----------------------------------------
# Required for the form to email you leads. Get a free key at https://resend.com
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Optional. Where consultation leads are delivered.
# Defaults to the business email in lib/site.ts (info@seniorsafetysolutions.ca).
# LEAD_TO_EMAIL=info@seniorsafetysolutions.ca

# Optional. The "from" address on lead emails.
# Before you verify a domain in Resend, leave this unset — the code falls back
# to Resend's test sender (onboarding@resend.dev), which delivers only to the
# email that owns your Resend account. Once your domain is verified in Resend,
# set this to an address on that domain, e.g.:
# LEAD_FROM_EMAIL=Edmonton Walk-In Bath Experts <website@yourdomain.ca>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public site URL is set in lib/site.ts (siteConfig.url). Update it there
# to your real domain before deploying to production.
